    "title": "Tor client started",
    "desc": "A program started the Tor client or enabled the tor service (the tor/torify/torsocks binaries, or systemctl/service starting tor). Routing traffic through Tor anonymises an attacker's command and control and defeats egress controls built around known destinations (MITRE T1090.003). A server or an agent account has no legitimate need for Tor, so starting it is a clean signal; tunnel_tool covers the other relays and port-forwards, this covers Tor specifically.",
